# CampusHub agent rules

Follow this file. Do not read paths listed in `.cursorignore` (dependencies, lockfiles, `dist/`, `build/`, coverage, logs, source maps).

## Stack

- Backend: TypeScript, Express, MongoDB via Mongoose. No other framework, ORM, or raw driver.
- Client: Vite + React + TypeScript in `client/` only. Use `fetch`. No axios unless asked.
- Do not add an npm package unless asked.
- No `.js` source. Backend `src/` is `.ts`. React components are `.tsx`. No `any`.

## Backend layers

| Layer | Path | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|---|
| Routes | `src/routes/` | Path wiring | Business logic, database |
| Controllers | `src/controllers/` | Parse the request, call a service, set status | Mongoose, try/catch |
| Middleware | `src/middleware/errorHandler.ts` | Turn thrown errors into HTTP JSON | Business rules |
| Services | `src/services/` | Business logic | `Request` / `Response` |
| Models | `src/models/` | Mongoose schemas | Business logic |
| Contracts | `src/types/contracts.ts` | Shared resource and reservation types | Express or React |

Controllers throw `AppError`. Express 5 forwards that rejection to `errorHandler`. Do not wrap each handler in try/catch.

## Client

- Functional components with an explicit props interface.
- Reservation fetching and submit state live in `client/src/hooks/useReservations.ts`.
- Do not call the API from JSX.
- Style with CSS modules.
- Import shared models from `src/types/contracts.ts`. Do not copy those interfaces into the client.
- Show `isLoading` and a visible error. A 409 uses: "This resource is already reserved for the selected time window".

## Commits

Imperative subject, under 10 words. Short body naming the rule that motivated the change. No emojis.
